---
deadlock_detection: true
options:
  max_actions: 200
  crash_on_yield: false
---
# kept.fizz -- a fizzbee model of how runs come by the views of chisel's
# cache that are kept between them: a run takes a kept view no other run has,
# or makes one, works in it and lets it go, and on its way in sweeps the
# views no run has taken for a day. cache.go is the code (take, lockKept,
# sweep, Release) with ../pool/pool.go's worker.enter; this is not a
# transcription of them and proves nothing of them line by line. It checks
# the protocol they are meant to follow. What a worker then does with its
# view during a pass is ../pool/views.fizz.
#
# two configurations, since three runs with everything is more states than
# the checker gets through in ten minutes:
#   pair (as written): two runs, two kept views, two days going by, one
#     run dying. 19009 states.
#   three: three runs, one kept view, one day going by, no run dying: a
#     run holding the view, one sweeping it and one after it. 56026 states.
#
# run:   make fizz    (the two, and the three designs that must fail)
# by hand, fizzbee 0.5.4:
#   timeout -k 10 600 fizz kept.fizz
#   timeout -k 10 600 fizz --preinit-hook "$THREE" kept.fizz
# with THREE the lines   W = 3   KEPT = 1   AGES = 1   CRASHES = 0
# A design that must fail is the pair and a line more:
#   DESIGN = "noverify"   fails K2
#   DESIGN = "nolock"     fails K3
#   INHERIT = False       fails K1
#
# requirements
#
# K1:  THE CACHE SHALL give a view to one run at a time: no two runs work
#      in one view at once, and no run works in a view where a chisel of a
#      run that died still runs.
# K2:  WHILE a run works in a view, THE CACHE SHALL keep the view where it
#      is: no sweep removes it.
# K3:  THE CACHE SHALL sweep a view only when it has gone a day without a
#      run taking it and no run has it.
# K4:  WHEN a run ends or dies, THE CACHE SHALL hold none of its views for
#      it: a lock has a live run behind it, or a chisel still running.
# K5:  THE CACHE SHALL let every run end: a run waits for no other run.
# K6:  THE CACHE SHALL make a view only for a run that found no kept one
#      free, so the views kept are no more than were ever wanted at once.
#
# invariants: K1, K2, K3, K4, K6. progress: K5.
#
# the boundary
#
# system: take and lockKept (list, open the lock file, lock it without
# waiting, look whether it is still the view's, touch), the making of a new
# view, sweep, Release.
# environment: time (a view goes a day untaken, whether a run has it or
# not), a run dying anywhere, and the chisel a run that died while cutting
# leaves running for a while.
#
# assumptions, each a thing the code can meet and the model does not
#
# - the lock is flock's: on the open file, so on the inode as it was when
#   opened, held by every process that has the open file, gone when the
#   last of them has closed it or died. Taking it never waits.
# - a rename of a view's dir is one step, and a file that was opened stays
#   lockable after its dir was renamed or removed.
# - a view is made under a name no run lists, locked, then renamed in one
#   step, so it is first seen kept and taken.
# - a run of a release that keeps no views does not know these: it sweeps
#   only the view-* dirs of its own kind, which a kept view is not.
# - the views are on one filesystem that keeps flock's promise. On one that
#   does not (some network mounts) two runs may take one view, as two
#   chisels in one cache.
#
# abstractions
#
# - a view is where it is: kept (under its name), trash (renamed away) or
#   gone. What it holds is not here: bringing a taken view up to date is
#   the run's own, with the lock held.
# - "stale" is a day gone since the view was last taken or let go. A run
#   that takes a view touches it.
# - a run sweeps at most one view, then takes one, works once, lets go.
# - a run that dies while its chisel runs leaves the chisel running in the
#   view until OrphanEnds. With INHERIT the chisel has the lock file open.
#
# what an atomic step merges
#
# every step of a run is one atomic block of the one Step action. A step
# holds one system call on what runs share (the dir of views, a lock), or
# what is the run's own.
# - sweep, pick: the listing of the dir and the open of one lock file. A
#   view renamed away between the two is one whose file does not open, the
#   same as one not listed.
# - sweep_lock, lock: flock without waiting.
# - sweep_verify, verify: the two stats and their comparison, with the
#   lock held: a view can only leave its place under its lock, so nothing
#   comes between them to any effect. The sweep also reads the view's time
#   again here.
# - sweep_rename: the rename to trash, then the close of the lock. The
#   removal of the trash is no one's to see.
# - take: the touch, then bringing the view up to date, under the lock.
# - work: the run's chisels start in the view.
# - release: the touch and the close of the lock.
#
# not modelled: what a view holds and how it is brought up to date, a view
# that cannot be made, new-* and trash-* dirs a dead run left (no run takes
# them: they are removed a day later), and runs that keep no views.
#
# decisions the model forced
#
# D1: a lock got is not yet a lock on a view. A run opens a view's lock
#     file, a sweep holding the lock renames the view away and lets go, and
#     the run's flock then succeeds on a file that is no view's: it works
#     in a dir being removed. DESIGN "noverify" is that and fails K2. The
#     design kept looks, once it has the lock, whether the file at the
#     view's path is still the one it holds.
# D2: a sweep that only looks at a view's time removes one a run has: the
#     time says when it was taken, not whether. DESIGN "nolock" fails K3.
#     The sweep takes the lock first and reads the time again with it.
# D3: a run that dies leaves its chisel running, and its lock is gone with
#     it: the next run takes the view and starts a chisel beside the old
#     one, two chisels in one cache, which views exist to prevent. INHERIT
#     False is that and fails K1. The chisel is started with the lock file
#     open (cut.Runner.Inherit), so the lock outlives the run by as long
#     as the chisel does.
#
# mutation runs, each a change to the model and the assertion that then
# fails:
#   sweep_fresh     the sweep does not read the time again     K3 OnlyStaleAndFreeIsSwept
#   no_touch        taking a view does not touch it            K3 OnlyStaleAndFreeIsSwept
#   no_unlock       a run ends with its lock held              K4 ALockHasALiveOwner
#   DESIGN "noverify"                                          K2 AViewInUseStays
#   DESIGN "nolock"                                            K3 OnlyStaleAndFreeIsSwept
#   INHERIT False                                              K1 OneRunAView

W = 2            # runs
KEPT = 2         # views kept from earlier runs, free at the start
AGES = 2         # times a view goes stale
CRASHES = 1      # runs that die
DESIGN = "verify"   # or "noverify", "nolock"
INHERIT = True      # a run's chisel holds the lock too
MUTANT = ""         # for the mutation runs: sweep_fresh, no_unlock, no_touch

def movable(r):
    return r.pc != "exit" and r.pc != "dead"

def all_over(runs):
    return len([r for r in runs if movable(r)]) == 0

action Init:
    # where: kept, trash, gone. holder: the run whose lock it is, -1 none.
    # holder -2 is a chisel a dead run left running. orphan: such a chisel
    # runs in the view.
    views = [record(where="kept", holder=-1, stale=False, orphan=False, dead_runs=False, used=False) for k in range(KEPT)]
    # fd: the view whose lock file the run has open, -1 none. tried: views
    # the run passed over this phase. sweeps: stale views it may still try.
    runs = [record(pc="sweep", fd=-1, view=-1, tried=[], swept=False) for i in range(W)]
    # witnesses
    used_twice = False      # two runs worked in one view at once
    used_gone = False       # a run worked in a view no longer kept
    bad_sweep = False       # a view went to the trash fresh, or held by another
    reuses = 0              # a kept view taken by a run
    sweeps = 0              # a stale view swept
    lost_races = 0          # a lock got on a view that had gone meanwhile
    made = 0                # views made new
    after_crash = False     # a view a dead run held was taken again
    orphan_held = False     # a run passed over a view a left chisel held
    ages = 0
    crashes = 0

# a day goes by for a view, taken or not
atomic action Age:
    require ages < AGES
    j = oneof [k for k in range(len(views)) if views[k].where == "kept" and not views[k].stale]
    views[j].stale = True
    views[j].used = False
    ages = ages + 1

# a run dies, wherever it is: its locks go with it, but for the one its
# chisel, still running, holds too
atomic action Crash:
    require crashes < CRASHES
    i = oneof [k for k in range(W) if movable(runs[k])]
    crashes = crashes + 1
    for k in range(len(views)):
        if views[k].holder == i:
            views[k].holder = -1
            if runs[i].pc == "release" and runs[i].view == k:
                views[k].orphan = True
                views[k].dead_runs = True
                if INHERIT:
                    views[k].holder = -2
    runs[i].pc = "dead"
    runs[i].fd = -1

atomic fair action OrphanEnds:
    j = oneof [k for k in range(len(views)) if views[k].orphan]
    views[j].orphan = False
    if views[j].holder == -2:
        views[j].holder = -1

atomic fair action Step:
    i = oneof [k for k in range(W) if movable(runs[k])]
    pc = runs[i].pc
    f = runs[i].fd
    if pc == "sweep":
        # one stale view at most, or none: then on to a view of its own
        cands = [k for k in range(len(views)) if views[k].where == "kept" and views[k].stale and k not in runs[i].tried]
        go = oneof [True, False]
        if len(cands) > 0 and go and not runs[i].swept:
            j = oneof cands
            runs[i].tried = runs[i].tried + [j]
            runs[i].fd = j
            if DESIGN == "nolock":
                runs[i].pc = "sweep_rename"
            else:
                runs[i].pc = "sweep_lock"
        else:
            runs[i].tried = []
            runs[i].pc = "pick"
    elif pc == "sweep_lock":
        if views[f].holder == -1:
            views[f].holder = i
            runs[i].pc = "sweep_verify"
        else:
            runs[i].fd = -1
            runs[i].pc = "sweep"
    elif pc == "sweep_verify":
        # the lock is on what was opened: is it still the kept view, and
        # still stale?
        if views[f].where == "kept" and (views[f].stale or MUTANT == "sweep_fresh"):
            runs[i].pc = "sweep_rename"
        else:
            views[f].holder = -1
            runs[i].fd = -1
            runs[i].pc = "sweep"
    elif pc == "sweep_rename":
        if views[f].where == "kept":
            if not views[f].stale or views[f].used or (views[f].holder != i and views[f].holder != -1):
                bad_sweep = True
            if len([r for r in runs if r.pc == "work" and r.view == f]) > 0:
                used_gone = True
            views[f].where = "trash"
            sweeps = sweeps + 1
        if views[f].holder == i:
            views[f].holder = -1
        runs[i].fd = -1
        runs[i].swept = True
        runs[i].pc = "sweep"
    elif pc == "pick":
        cands = [k for k in range(len(views)) if views[k].where == "kept" and k not in runs[i].tried]
        if len(cands) > 0:
            j = oneof cands
            runs[i].tried = runs[i].tried + [j]
            runs[i].fd = j
            runs[i].pc = "lock"
        else:
            # made under a name no one lists, locked, then renamed: it
            # appears kept and held at once
            views = views + [record(where="kept", holder=i, stale=False, orphan=False, dead_runs=False, used=False)]
            runs[i].view = len(views) - 1
            made = made + 1
            runs[i].pc = "work"
    elif pc == "lock":
        if views[f].holder == -2:
            orphan_held = True
        if views[f].holder == -1:
            views[f].holder = i
            if DESIGN == "noverify":
                runs[i].pc = "take"
            else:
                runs[i].pc = "verify"
        else:
            runs[i].fd = -1
            runs[i].pc = "pick"
    elif pc == "verify":
        if views[f].where == "kept":
            runs[i].pc = "take"
        else:
            lost_races = lost_races + 1
            views[f].holder = -1
            runs[i].fd = -1
            runs[i].pc = "pick"
    elif pc == "take":
        # touched, synced with the shared cache: the run's own from here
        if views[f].where == "kept" and MUTANT != "no_touch":
            views[f].stale = False
        views[f].used = True
        if views[f].dead_runs:
            after_crash = True
        runs[i].view = f
        runs[i].fd = -1
        reuses = reuses + 1
        runs[i].pc = "work"
    elif pc == "work":
        v = runs[i].view
        if views[v].where != "kept":
            used_gone = True
        if len([k for k in range(W) if k != i and runs[k].pc in ["work", "release"] and runs[k].view == v]) > 0:
            used_twice = True
        # its chisel starts, beside one a dead run left there?
        if views[v].orphan:
            used_twice = True
        runs[i].pc = "release"
    elif pc == "release":
        v = runs[i].view
        if MUTANT != "no_unlock":
            views[v].holder = -1
        runs[i].pc = "exit"

atomic action Finished:
    require all_over(runs)
    pass

# K1
always assertion OneRunAView:
    if used_twice:
        return False
    for a in range(W):
        for b in range(W):
            if a < b and runs[a].pc in ["work", "release"] and runs[b].pc in ["work", "release"] and runs[a].view == runs[b].view:
                return False
    return True

# K2
always assertion AViewInUseStays:
    if used_gone:
        return False
    for r in runs:
        if r.pc in ["work", "release"] and views[r.view].where != "kept":
            return False
    return True

# K3
always assertion OnlyStaleAndFreeIsSwept:
    return not bad_sweep

# K4
always assertion ALockHasALiveOwner:
    for v in views:
        if v.holder >= 0 and not movable(runs[v.holder]):
            return False
        if v.holder == -2 and not v.orphan:
            return False
    return True

# K5
always eventually assertion EveryRunEnds:
    return all_over(runs)

# K6: a view is made only when no kept one could be had
always assertion NoMoreViewsThanRuns:
    return len([v for v in views if v.where == "kept"]) <= KEPT + W

exists assertion AKeptViewIsReused:
    return reuses > 0

exists assertion EveryKeptViewIsReused:
    return reuses >= min(KEPT, W)

exists assertion ALeftChiselHoldsItsView:
    return CRASHES == 0 or not INHERIT or orphan_held

exists assertion AStaleViewIsSwept:
    return AGES == 0 or sweeps > 0

exists assertion ALockOnAGoneViewIsDropped:
    return DESIGN != "verify" or AGES == 0 or lost_races > 0

exists assertion AViewIsMade:
    return made > 0

exists assertion ADeadRunsViewIsTakenAgain:
    return CRASHES == 0 or after_crash

exists assertion EveryRunWorks:
    return len([r for r in runs if r.pc == "exit"]) == W
